# OpenMC Studio -- core runtime requirements
#
# Version RANGES are used deliberately instead of exact pins: this lets
# pip resolve whatever compatible version fits your own Python install,
# rather than forcing one exact snapshot tied to one development
# machine. scipy is NOT listed explicitly -- it is pulled in
# automatically as one of openmc's own dependencies, so pip resolves a
# version compatible with your OpenMC and Python versions rather than a
# version pinned to a Python-3.12-only release.
#
# This list was built by directly reviewing the imports in every module
# in the project (main_window, script_editor, project_tree,
# property_editor, console_widget, materials_page, material_editor,
# nuclide_editor, geometry_page, settings_page, tallies_page,
# libraries_page, plots_page, voxel_page, tracks_page) rather than
# copied from a pip-freeze snapshot.

